course: dictionary
lesson: 8865
title: Shopping: one word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Shopping can mean three things, and the words around it show you which one. «Dad is going shopping after school.» Here shopping means going to shops to buy things.
explain: «Mum put the shopping away in the fridge.» Now shopping means the things she bought, especially food. The clue is put away in the fridge, because you cannot put a trip to the shops in a fridge.
explain: «Grandma likes shopping online at night.» Here shopping means buying things on the internet. To check, swap your meaning into the sentence. Going to the shops online does not make sense, so the meaning must be buying online.
fact: Shopping means going to shops to buy things.
fact: In British English, «the shopping» means the things you have bought, especially food.
fact: Shopping can also mean buying things online.
fact: Shop is the verb: shop, shops, shopped, shopping.
fact: Useful phrases: «go shopping», «do the shopping», «shopping list», and «window shopping», which means looking at things without buying them.
exercise: «At a self-checkout you scan your own shopping.» What does shopping mean here? | *The things you have bought | A type of shopping bag | Going to the shops with a friend | Buying a present for someone
exercise: «A rolling shopping trolley is stopped by an adult, because children can tip over and hit cars.» What is a shopping trolley? | A bag you carry on your back | A cart for carrying your things around a shop | *A cart for carrying your things around a shop, with wheels | A bus that goes to the shops
exercise: Dad says, «I will do the shopping this afternoon.» What does he mean? | Read a book about shops | *Go to the shops and buy food and things | Watch a film at the cinema | Clean the house from top to bottom
test: «Shopping hungry makes everyone grab extra.» What does shopping mean here? | The things you have bought | *Going to the shops to buy things | Buying things online | A shopping list
test: Which phrase means writing down the things you need before you go to the shops? | Do the shopping | Shopping trolley | Window shopping | *Shopping list
exam: Mia says, «Grandma does her shopping online.» What does shopping mean here? | *Buying things on the internet | Looking in shop windows | The things she has bought | Going to the shops on foot
